@startuml
title D&D Simple - Tactical Board Realtime Sync

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor "Player A" as PlayerA
participant "TacticalBoardPage A" as BoardA
participant "useRoomSocket A" as SocketHookA
participant "Socket.IO Server" as Socket
database "PostgreSQL\nRoom.boardState" as DB
participant "TacticalBoardPage B\n(useRoomSocket)" as BoardB

note over BoardA, BoardB
Both clients are already authenticated and have joined
the same Socket.IO room with room:join.
end note

PlayerA -> BoardA: Move token or change board state
BoardA -> SocketHookA: Debounced room board snapshot
SocketHookA -> Socket: board:state({ boardState, baseUpdatedAt })
Socket -> DB: getRoom(roomCode)
DB --> Socket: Room with current boardState and updatedAt

alt baseUpdatedAt is stale
  Socket -> SocketHookA: board:update({ boardState, updatedAt })
  Socket --> SocketHookA: callback error + latest boardState
  SocketHookA -> BoardA: Resynchronize local board
else update is authorized and current
  Socket -> Socket: authorizeBoardStateSync(...)
  Socket -> DB: saveRoomBoardState(room.code, boardState)
  DB --> Socket: Updated Room snapshot
  Socket -> SocketHookA: board:update({ boardState, updatedAt })
  Socket -> BoardB: board:update({ boardState, updatedAt })
  Socket --> SocketHookA: callback ok + updatedAt
  SocketHookA -> BoardA: Render latest board snapshot
  BoardB -> BoardB: Render latest board snapshot
end

note over Socket
Turn advancement uses board:advance-turn
and then broadcasts board:update after persistence.
end note

@enduml
